WEBVTT

00:43.043 --> 00:48.424
CHAPTER 8: I'M SURE IT WAS MY GLASSES
YOU TROD ON EARLIER

00:51.719 --> 00:54.054
EPISODE 3

00:58.142 --> 01:00.311
Looks like he's on his way
to catch the bus.

01:01.645 --> 01:04.690
Am I going to run into him
every time I go to school?

01:06.859 --> 01:08.944
He's a teacher. He should leave earlier.

01:20.956 --> 01:22.750
Get a move on.

01:36.847 --> 01:37.973
What's he doing?

01:51.779 --> 01:52.863
Mr. Ga!

01:54.406 --> 01:55.574
Mr. Ga!

01:56.909 --> 01:59.036
Mr. Ga! Are you okay?

01:59.119 --> 02:00.371
Mr. Ga!

02:01.121 --> 02:03.082
Mr. Ga!

02:07.795 --> 02:09.505
What's that?

02:10.089 --> 02:11.257
Is that bird poop?

02:13.175 --> 02:15.135
Gross!

02:27.690 --> 02:29.275
Mr. Ga?

02:29.900 --> 02:31.277
Mr. Ga!

02:31.360 --> 02:32.361
Mr. Ga.

02:33.153 --> 02:33.988
Sir…

02:37.116 --> 02:38.576
I don't think he's breathing.

02:43.873 --> 02:46.208
Mr. Ga! Wake up.

02:46.292 --> 02:47.293
What do I do?

02:50.087 --> 02:51.171
Mr. Ga!

02:53.007 --> 02:55.092
Man, he is not breathing!

02:55.175 --> 02:56.468
What do I do?

03:07.730 --> 03:08.981
Come on, Eui-ju.

03:09.064 --> 03:12.234
You're doing this to save a life.

03:21.327 --> 03:22.202
Mr. Ga?

03:23.704 --> 03:24.538
Mr. Ga.

03:25.164 --> 03:26.582
Are you okay?

03:26.665 --> 03:27.499
Mr. Ga.

03:29.376 --> 03:30.252
Are you…

03:32.212 --> 03:33.839
It's me, sir. Yeo Eui-ju.

03:34.798 --> 03:35.758
Are you okay?

03:46.101 --> 03:47.394
What are you doing here?

03:49.980 --> 03:51.357
What do you mean?

03:51.440 --> 03:54.109
How can you say that to the person
who just saved your life?

03:54.777 --> 03:57.780
Anyway, why did you pass out here?

03:57.863 --> 04:00.950
Surely not just because
of some pigeon poop?

04:03.953 --> 04:07.206
Pigeon droppings not only carry avian flu
and other infectious diseases,

04:07.289 --> 04:10.209
but also contain ammonia and acids
strong enough to damage concrete.

04:10.834 --> 04:11.752
"Just because"?

04:16.215 --> 04:17.299
Have you lost something?

04:18.842 --> 04:19.885
Oh, your glasses.

04:20.886 --> 04:21.929
Shall I help you look?

04:23.514 --> 04:24.348
Sure.

04:24.974 --> 04:25.933
Okay.

04:51.500 --> 04:53.419
What was that sound?

04:53.502 --> 04:54.837
Did you just step on my glasses?

04:56.046 --> 04:57.548
No.

04:57.631 --> 04:59.299
No, don't be silly.

05:00.134 --> 05:02.469
I was just…

05:03.554 --> 05:04.847
I mean…

05:04.930 --> 05:07.099
I just stepped on a branch, that's all.

05:08.183 --> 05:10.019
-That was the crack of it snapping.
-What time is it?

05:10.102 --> 05:11.854
-Sorry?
-What time is it?

05:16.817 --> 05:18.610
It's 7:40 a.m.

05:19.987 --> 05:21.572
Will you call Dong-ju?

05:24.283 --> 05:25.117
Sure.

05:27.870 --> 05:29.204
It's locked.

05:30.831 --> 05:31.749
Okay.

05:32.416 --> 05:33.459
Here you are.

05:34.752 --> 05:36.503
Is your vision that bad?

05:37.838 --> 05:38.881
It's me.

05:39.840 --> 05:42.885
If you go to my room, my spare glasses
are in the first drawer of my desk.

05:42.968 --> 05:44.011
Can you bring them to me?

05:45.179 --> 05:47.056
Yeah, I'm near the bus stop.

05:48.223 --> 05:49.058
Okay.

05:51.727 --> 05:52.811
Where have they gotten to?

05:58.025 --> 06:01.653
I told you to carpool with us.
Ignoring me always leads to trouble.

06:02.821 --> 06:04.156
What do I do?

06:04.239 --> 06:05.866
Shall I just chuck them somewhere?

06:10.329 --> 06:11.205
Oh, I found 500 won!

06:12.414 --> 06:13.957
Come on!

06:15.000 --> 06:16.168
Let's go or we'll be late.

06:16.251 --> 06:19.505
If we haven't found them by now,
they're not here.

06:20.422 --> 06:23.926
I'm sure someone saw them and took them.

06:24.009 --> 06:25.886
They recognized how expensive they were.

06:25.969 --> 06:27.513
-Don't you think?
-Yes.

06:27.596 --> 06:28.639
-Yes.
-Right?

06:30.849 --> 06:32.392
See you at school.

06:40.359 --> 06:41.443
What's with that look?

06:49.034 --> 06:50.160
Is she hoping for a lift?

07:02.923 --> 07:04.341
Darn it.

07:05.551 --> 07:06.635
Sorry, it's so cramped.

07:07.511 --> 07:10.097
No, it's fine.

07:10.180 --> 07:11.515
I'm just grateful for the lift.

07:20.440 --> 07:22.568
THIS IS CRAZY!

07:23.277 --> 07:25.612
This is crazy!
I'm in the teachers' car right now.

07:25.696 --> 07:28.407
Mr. Jung's driving, and I'm stuck between
Mr. Noh and Mr. Yoon.

07:28.490 --> 07:29.366
No way!

07:33.871 --> 07:34.872
How'd that happen?

07:36.623 --> 07:38.709
There was a whole thing.
I'll tell you later.

07:42.629 --> 07:43.881
I'm putting my seat back.

07:47.801 --> 07:48.677
Okay.

07:52.598 --> 07:54.099
I knew it.

07:54.183 --> 07:58.353
Mr. Ga knows no one but himself
and sweet Mr. Yoon doesn't say anything.

08:01.481 --> 08:02.858
Were you up all night again?

08:06.069 --> 08:08.530
It's because you wouldn't let him sleep.

08:08.614 --> 08:11.867
-Don't you know he's a sleepyhead?
-I didn't do it on purpose.

08:12.451 --> 08:14.912
He wanted another round. That's all.

08:15.829 --> 08:17.497
It doesn't matter
how much you're enjoying it,

08:17.581 --> 08:18.790
make sure he gets his rest.

08:19.291 --> 08:20.125
Got it?

08:21.710 --> 08:22.669
Unbelievable!

08:22.753 --> 08:24.713
What can they have been doing all night?

08:25.214 --> 08:28.008
God, forgive me.

08:28.091 --> 08:30.219
I'll go to hell after writing this!

08:36.183 --> 08:37.142
What's wrong?

08:38.810 --> 08:40.562
Are you hot? Shall I put the AC on?

08:41.146 --> 08:41.980
No.

08:42.898 --> 08:44.233
There's no need.

08:49.905 --> 08:51.990
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

08:57.246 --> 08:59.289
Who are you to ride in his car?

08:59.373 --> 09:01.583
Cat got your tongue? Answer me!

09:01.667 --> 09:04.586
-Say something!
-How dare you!

09:07.589 --> 09:08.715
What's wrong with her?

09:09.925 --> 09:11.093
Just a moment, sir.

09:11.176 --> 09:12.261
If they see me in here,

09:12.344 --> 09:14.513
they're going to kill me.

09:14.596 --> 09:16.723
Hey, it's Mr. Jung!

09:19.059 --> 09:21.270
No, this can't be happening.

09:21.353 --> 09:22.604
No!

09:22.688 --> 09:25.315
If the other kids find out I'm here,
I'm dead meat.

09:25.399 --> 09:26.358
What do I do?

10:34.634 --> 10:35.761
I need more oxygen.

10:44.102 --> 10:46.605
I can't say that didn't hurt.

10:47.814 --> 10:49.149
Still, he saved my life.

10:54.404 --> 10:57.449
It's because you wouldn't let me sleep.

10:58.200 --> 10:59.951
You know I'm a sleepyhead.

11:02.621 --> 11:04.831
They're the one true pair.

11:15.550 --> 11:16.593
Aren't you getting out?

11:21.264 --> 11:22.140
Hey.

11:23.100 --> 11:23.934
Yes?

11:25.977 --> 11:26.937
Tell me the truth.

11:28.230 --> 11:29.147
About what?

11:30.107 --> 11:32.109
Whichever way I look at it,

11:32.776 --> 11:34.986
I'm sure it was my glasses
you trod on earlier.

11:36.154 --> 11:37.072
No, it wasn't.

11:39.324 --> 11:42.160
If you're lying to me,
you're going to regret it.

11:42.744 --> 11:44.871
I'm really not.

11:45.872 --> 11:47.958
-Where's your essay?
-I'm working on it.

11:55.715 --> 11:58.260
CHAPTER 9:
HI! I'M JENNY

11:58.844 --> 12:01.847
-Good morning, Mr. Ga!
-Good morning, Mr. Ga!

12:03.723 --> 12:04.558
Come in.

12:04.641 --> 12:06.226
-Who is it?
-A transfer?

12:12.983 --> 12:16.862
We have an exchange student joining us
for the rest of the semester.

12:20.866 --> 12:22.993
Hi! I'm Jenny.

12:23.827 --> 12:26.705
I'm here on exchange from Singapore.

12:26.788 --> 12:28.457
Nice to meet you all.

12:28.540 --> 12:31.209
I'm really excited to be here, so

12:31.293 --> 12:33.462
I hope we'll have a lot of fun together.

12:35.672 --> 12:36.923
Welcome, Jenny!

12:37.424 --> 12:38.425
She's so cute.

12:38.508 --> 12:39.342
You can sit there.

12:42.846 --> 12:44.890
-Hey, Jenny.
-Hello.

12:44.973 --> 12:46.099
Hello.

12:48.059 --> 12:49.144
Hello.

12:50.562 --> 12:51.605
Hi!

12:56.443 --> 12:59.613
She's probably not used to Korean culture
or Korean schools,

12:59.696 --> 13:00.864
so look after her.

13:00.947 --> 13:02.073
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

13:02.157 --> 13:03.158
Dismissed.

13:03.783 --> 13:05.785
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

13:07.370 --> 13:08.246
Jenny.

13:08.330 --> 13:10.373
-Hi!
-Hello!

13:10.457 --> 13:11.833
Hello!

13:11.917 --> 13:13.835
-Hey!
-Hello!

13:13.919 --> 13:16.171
My name is Yeo Eui-ju.

13:16.254 --> 13:17.547
Do you speak Korean well?

13:18.548 --> 13:20.926
Yes. Okay, maybe like…

13:21.551 --> 13:23.220
I can't speak that much Korean.

13:23.303 --> 13:24.971
But I'm learning.

13:25.555 --> 13:27.849
If you help me,
I'm sure I'll soon pick it up.

13:29.059 --> 13:31.144
My name is Go-ya.

13:31.228 --> 13:32.187
Nice to meet you.

13:32.270 --> 13:34.439
Nice to meet you.

13:35.565 --> 13:39.736
Jenny, why did you come to Korea?

13:41.154 --> 13:43.490
Doesn't everybody want to come to Korea?

13:44.115 --> 13:45.784
There's lots of yummy food.

13:45.867 --> 13:49.746
And I wanted to visit the places
I've seen in K-dramas.

13:49.829 --> 13:51.831
-I see.
-That's right.

13:51.915 --> 13:53.291
That makes sense.

13:53.375 --> 13:58.129
Then why did you come to Jeonju
and not Seoul?

13:58.838 --> 14:01.925
I did apply to a school in Seoul.

14:02.425 --> 14:03.260
But…

14:03.343 --> 14:04.970
I was on the computer, and I was like…

14:08.557 --> 14:09.766
I clicked on the wrong one.

14:09.849 --> 14:11.059
-You…
-You clicked on the wrong…

14:11.142 --> 14:12.936
-Oh, she clicked on the wrong one!
-Oh, she clicked on the wrong one!

14:13.520 --> 14:14.771
You selected this school by mistake.

14:14.854 --> 14:18.358
But it's okay. This place is great, like…

14:18.441 --> 14:19.901
Jeonju is really pretty.

14:19.985 --> 14:22.279
-Yeah, it really is.
-It's great!

14:22.362 --> 14:26.157
CHAPTER 10:
I'M GOING TO TUMBLE YOU AROUND

14:28.410 --> 14:29.286
Darn it.

14:34.791 --> 14:36.418
Is it because he switched glasses?

14:38.795 --> 14:40.130
Why does he look sick?

14:49.139 --> 14:50.974
Why won't this stick?

14:52.225 --> 14:53.935
Shall I just throw them away
and feign ignorance?

14:56.271 --> 14:57.814
I can't do that.

14:57.897 --> 14:59.608
I have to give them back.

15:00.483 --> 15:02.944
It seems like his spare ones
aren't the right strength.

15:04.863 --> 15:07.449
Come on, help me out here.

15:07.532 --> 15:09.326
Type one verbs

15:09.409 --> 15:13.872
refers to almost all verbs
that do not end in "ru."

15:13.955 --> 15:16.625
So, the verb "iku" will become "ikanai."

15:16.708 --> 15:18.668
You add "a" to the "ku" form.

15:18.752 --> 15:20.629
Type two verbs are much easier.

15:20.712 --> 15:22.464
All you have to do is take off the "ru."

15:24.174 --> 15:27.052
So it will become "tabenai."

15:28.428 --> 15:29.804
As for type three verbs…

15:35.018 --> 15:39.064
I'M TRULY SORRY

15:46.613 --> 15:48.198
JAPANESE LANGUAGE

15:52.702 --> 15:54.871
During my class…

15:57.666 --> 15:59.668
You're not paying attention to me?

16:01.711 --> 16:03.338
I cannot believe it.

16:15.517 --> 16:16.351
How are you feeling?

16:17.435 --> 16:20.271
Like I've been watching
the Mandelbrot set zooming out

16:21.064 --> 16:22.941
at ultra-high speed all day.

16:23.733 --> 16:24.609
Mandel…

16:26.778 --> 16:27.862
I said I feel dizzy.

16:29.614 --> 16:31.866
I see.

16:37.664 --> 16:38.665
Come in.

16:47.424 --> 16:49.175
I caught one of your students

16:49.259 --> 16:53.054
doing homework you assigned
during my Japanese class.

16:54.180 --> 16:55.849
You deal with it, Mr. Ga.

17:05.108 --> 17:05.984
Read it.

17:06.568 --> 17:07.819
Sorry?

17:09.028 --> 17:11.740
Can't you just read it?

17:11.823 --> 17:13.658
All the other teachers are here.

17:24.127 --> 17:25.420
"Dear Euclid."

17:26.171 --> 17:27.213
I can't hear you.

17:29.716 --> 17:30.717
"Hello."

17:33.428 --> 17:34.262
"I…

17:35.555 --> 17:38.975
live in Jeonju in the year 2026,

17:39.058 --> 17:42.562
and my name is Yeo Eui-ju,
and I am 18 years old."

17:46.524 --> 17:49.319
"When I was in seventh grade,

17:50.028 --> 17:53.156
I was humiliated in front of my classmates
while solving a proof problem."

17:53.740 --> 17:55.658
"The shame of that

17:55.742 --> 17:58.203
led me to give up on math."

17:59.162 --> 18:03.166
"Why were you so obsessed with proofs?"

18:03.249 --> 18:05.960
"Are things that can't be proven
totally useless?"

18:06.544 --> 18:10.757
"If I'd been born before you, would I have
been spared from that kind of torment?"

18:14.385 --> 18:16.554
Is this an apology or a complaint?

18:20.141 --> 18:22.185
"Nevertheless,

18:22.977 --> 18:27.023
I can't help but admire
the first sentence of your book,

18:27.106 --> 18:29.526
'A point is that which has no parts.'"

18:30.527 --> 18:34.322
"Even someone like me who gave up on math
can understand that in one go."

18:34.948 --> 18:36.449
"Sir,

18:36.533 --> 18:41.579
I'm truly sorry for hurting you
with my ignorance,

18:41.663 --> 18:43.206
and for that I apologize…"

18:44.624 --> 18:45.834
That's as far as I've got.

18:46.876 --> 18:49.712
If you're going to write it during class,
don't bother. Two demerits.

18:50.713 --> 18:52.340
What? You think that's unfair?

18:53.925 --> 18:55.051
No, sir.

18:56.761 --> 18:58.555
I think taking care of your friends

18:58.638 --> 19:01.474
is one of the most important things
you learn at school.

19:04.686 --> 19:06.521
Starting today, you take care of Ji-a.

19:06.604 --> 19:09.941
From now on, if Choi Ji-a is absent, late,
or not at her desk during homeroom,

19:10.024 --> 19:11.734
I will give her two demerit points,

19:11.818 --> 19:12.777
and you four.

19:15.321 --> 19:16.573
-Sorry?
-Go.

19:17.824 --> 19:19.284
You can't do that!

19:20.118 --> 19:21.119
Mr. Ga!

19:23.746 --> 19:25.290
I can't.

19:25.373 --> 19:26.416
But, sir…

19:29.377 --> 19:30.503
Darn.

19:33.840 --> 19:35.758
Wow, that's ridiculous.

19:35.842 --> 19:38.052
How can you get more demerits than Ji-a?

19:38.136 --> 19:41.180
Why does he only ever pick on you?

19:41.264 --> 19:42.682
That's totally unfair.

19:42.765 --> 19:44.475
Wait, surely not.

19:44.559 --> 19:45.727
Do you think he likes you?

19:48.021 --> 19:50.565
Or maybe you look like his ex-girlfriend?

19:50.648 --> 19:53.192
He's picking on you
because every time he sees you,

19:53.276 --> 19:54.569
it reminds him of being dumped.

19:54.652 --> 19:56.487
What if it turns out

19:56.571 --> 20:00.116
your parents and his parents
are mortal enemies?

20:01.492 --> 20:03.786
Guys, just give it a rest.

20:03.870 --> 20:06.998
Maybe he just doesn't like your face.

20:07.081 --> 20:08.166
That could be it!

20:09.125 --> 20:10.168
Hey!

20:12.128 --> 20:13.004
Let's try something.

20:15.673 --> 20:17.842
-Good afternoon, Mr. Ga.
-Good afternoon, Mr. Ga.

20:19.302 --> 20:20.511
Where did we get to last time?

20:21.512 --> 20:22.722
Mr. Ga,

20:23.306 --> 20:25.224
Eui-ju isn't feeling very well.

20:27.018 --> 20:27.977
What's wrong with her?

20:30.688 --> 20:32.732
I don't know, sir.

20:33.733 --> 20:35.193
I feel dizzy and nauseous.

20:35.276 --> 20:37.987
And, gosh, I'm feeling so weak.

20:39.572 --> 20:40.531
Oh, no.

20:41.115 --> 20:42.325
What am I going to do?

20:42.951 --> 20:45.495
I can't take it.

20:45.578 --> 20:47.497
I think I'm dying.

20:58.424 --> 20:59.258
Yeo Eui-ju.

21:00.635 --> 21:01.719
Yes?

21:02.762 --> 21:04.681
Define left-hand limit
and right-hand limit.

21:06.057 --> 21:06.933
Sorry?

21:21.948 --> 21:26.035
If both the left-hand and right-hand limit
exist but aren't equal, does the limit

21:26.119 --> 21:27.120
exist or not?

21:27.787 --> 21:28.621
Sorry?

21:28.705 --> 21:30.540
If there's a single point
separated from a graph,

21:30.623 --> 21:32.250
what kind of discontinuity is that?

21:33.334 --> 21:37.130
What conditions do we need to prove
that f(x) is continuous at x equals a?

21:41.175 --> 21:42.677
Didn't we cover this last class?

21:42.760 --> 21:44.220
Were you even listening?

21:44.303 --> 21:46.180
If you'd revised
instead of faking being sick,

21:46.264 --> 21:47.807
you'd be able to answer.

21:51.227 --> 21:52.061
What are you doing here?

21:55.898 --> 21:58.067
I thought you wanted
to take Discrete Math together.

21:58.151 --> 21:59.861
Cut!

22:06.826 --> 22:08.119
Ju Si-on!

22:09.120 --> 22:09.996
Yes?

22:10.079 --> 22:13.166
Isn't that what I told you last time?
Were you even listening?

22:14.876 --> 22:15.752
You guys were great.

22:16.461 --> 22:18.129
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

22:18.212 --> 22:21.591
Do you not get the meaning
between the lines?

22:23.217 --> 22:26.012
Here, Yoon is talking to Tae-ha,
and you're supposed to feel

22:26.095 --> 22:27.597
angry and jealous, but…

22:27.680 --> 22:30.558
Yoon has already agreed
to take one of your classes with you.

22:30.641 --> 22:33.269
You know
you're on a different level to Tae-ha.

22:33.352 --> 22:36.314
You're supposed
to radiate an air of superiority!

22:36.397 --> 22:37.774
Are you not capable of that?

22:38.524 --> 22:39.567
I think I did.

22:43.029 --> 22:44.822
How dare you answer back!

22:48.159 --> 22:51.162
I'm the writer,
and you're just a character.

22:51.245 --> 22:52.163
Get it?

22:52.246 --> 22:54.540
I'm the writer, and you're just a teach…

22:57.710 --> 22:58.544
Hang on.

23:00.171 --> 23:02.256
You're just a character.

23:03.841 --> 23:06.969
Why do you always go off script
and do what you want?

23:07.053 --> 23:12.100
Every last period of my writing has soul!

23:13.017 --> 23:16.729
So stop whining and do exactly what I say!

23:16.813 --> 23:18.272
Yes, ma'am.

23:19.482 --> 23:20.858
What are you fuming about?

23:28.116 --> 23:31.536
Write the basic concepts of functions
ten times each.

23:32.537 --> 23:33.704
Yes, sir.

23:38.751 --> 23:40.920
Mr. Full-of-regrets Ju Si-on.

23:41.003 --> 23:42.130
Just you wait and see.

23:42.213 --> 23:45.508
I'm going to tumble you around.

23:46.134 --> 23:47.510
Round and around.

23:47.593 --> 23:50.805
CHAPTER 11:
HE NEVER LIKED ME TO BEGIN WITH

23:50.888 --> 23:52.265
Is this a pork cutlet?

23:53.015 --> 23:53.975
-It's a fish cutlet.
-Jenny.

23:54.058 --> 23:55.977
Is the food okay?

23:56.060 --> 23:57.687
-It's pretty tasty.
-It is, isn't it?

23:58.396 --> 24:00.773
If you enjoy it too much, you'll get fat.

24:02.692 --> 24:04.402
-Just eat up.
-Hey, Jenny.

24:04.986 --> 24:06.112
Do you have a boyfriend?

24:06.195 --> 24:07.530
Yes.

24:10.199 --> 24:11.284
He's Brazilian.

24:11.367 --> 24:12.952
Brazilian?

24:13.035 --> 24:14.203
His name is Luiz.

24:14.912 --> 24:16.330
So global.

24:17.039 --> 24:18.207
How did you meet him?

24:18.791 --> 24:20.626
At the Louvre in Paris.

24:20.710 --> 24:22.253
He's studying photography at college.

24:22.336 --> 24:24.672
He kept asking me to be his model.

24:24.755 --> 24:27.175
So, that's how we started dating.

24:28.509 --> 24:30.261
So, he's in France right now?

24:30.344 --> 24:31.387
Yeah.

24:32.180 --> 24:33.097
You must miss him.

24:33.181 --> 24:34.140
Yeah.

24:34.724 --> 24:36.184
He said since I left,

24:36.267 --> 24:38.978
he's completely lost his appetite.

24:39.061 --> 24:41.314
He said he doesn't smile much either.

24:41.939 --> 24:43.149
Isn't that funny?

24:43.733 --> 24:44.901
Brazilian guys are different.

24:44.984 --> 24:46.319
How would you know?

24:46.402 --> 24:48.070
How would I not?

24:49.113 --> 24:53.492
Jenny, what did your boyfriend say
when he asked you to model for him?

24:54.869 --> 24:56.621
Excuse me.

24:57.205 --> 24:59.916
I've been searching for the perfect
golden hour light all day.

25:00.499 --> 25:04.545
But I've ended up finding something
even more beautiful.

25:05.129 --> 25:08.966
Let me capture this beautiful moment.

25:11.469 --> 25:12.929
That's so romantic.

25:17.516 --> 25:21.938
YUL EYE CLINIC

25:22.521 --> 25:25.024
PRESCRIPTION

25:39.372 --> 25:44.085
BUBU PHARMACY

25:45.336 --> 25:47.213
There's seven days-worth.

25:47.964 --> 25:49.924
Take them three times a day.

25:50.007 --> 25:52.426
This is the anti-inflammatory
and this is for your stomach.

25:52.510 --> 25:53.636
-Okay.
-And,

25:53.719 --> 25:55.972
your eye medicine is a steroid,

25:56.055 --> 25:58.307
so make sure you shake it before use.

25:58.891 --> 26:00.142
That'll be 9,600 won.

26:02.478 --> 26:04.355
Your eyes are really bloodshot.

26:04.981 --> 26:07.984
Since you're wearing glasses,
I guess you didn't get LASIK.

26:08.067 --> 26:09.443
You'd better change your glasses.

26:09.527 --> 26:11.279
Our eyes are so important.

26:43.352 --> 26:44.729
I'm sorry.

26:45.479 --> 26:48.107
I was just reminded of that thing.

26:48.190 --> 26:49.275
You know in cartoons,

26:49.358 --> 26:51.944
when the main character
takes off their glasses,

26:52.028 --> 26:54.196
and they're transformed
into someone really handsome.

26:59.201 --> 27:01.579
You really should wear lenses if you can.

27:05.374 --> 27:06.417
Bye!

27:11.964 --> 27:13.466
A man straight out of a comic.

27:14.884 --> 27:15.926
A man straight out of a comic.

27:22.892 --> 27:24.518
AFTER-SCHOOL PROGRAM APPLICATION

27:24.602 --> 27:26.771
Get your parents' signatures
and bring it back to me.

27:26.854 --> 27:27.688
Yes, sir.

27:37.698 --> 27:38.949
What the heck?

27:39.033 --> 27:40.076
Is he sick?

27:42.328 --> 27:43.287
What did the doctor say?

27:45.831 --> 27:47.833
It'll take at least two weeks
to get new glasses.

27:48.334 --> 27:49.210
Two weeks?

27:49.877 --> 27:51.504
How are you going to cope for that long?

27:55.758 --> 27:56.717
Well done.

27:56.801 --> 27:58.677
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

28:07.269 --> 28:08.270
Ji-a!

28:08.354 --> 28:09.688
Ji-a, where are you going?

28:10.606 --> 28:12.191
You have to wait for the final bell.

28:13.442 --> 28:14.485
Are you off to work?

28:14.568 --> 28:16.237
Can't you wait until the bell rings?

28:16.320 --> 28:19.698
From now on, if you come in late
or leave early, I will get demerits.

28:21.951 --> 28:22.910
Hey!

28:22.993 --> 28:25.371
I asked nicely.
Can't you just do me a solid?

28:27.289 --> 28:28.916
Do you think I want to do this?

28:36.215 --> 28:37.633
Mr. Ga! Did you see that?

28:37.716 --> 28:40.219
I clearly told Ji-a not to go.

28:40.302 --> 28:43.305
But she didn't listen and just left.

28:47.601 --> 28:50.646
Can't you just count this
as me having done it?

28:50.729 --> 28:52.940
There's really nothing I can do.

28:55.860 --> 28:56.777
Yeo Eui-ju.

28:58.863 --> 29:00.156
Four demerit points.

29:09.165 --> 29:12.710
GENERAL WASTE

29:14.545 --> 29:15.796
Go-ya was right.

29:16.422 --> 29:18.048
Things were screwed up from the start.

29:18.632 --> 29:20.718
He just never liked me.

29:25.890 --> 29:28.100
I saw you filming. Delete it.

29:28.184 --> 29:30.811
I want you to write a letter to Euclid.
Twenty pages.

29:32.521 --> 29:33.397
Yeo Eui-ju.

29:34.148 --> 29:35.316
Four demerit points.

30:56.855 --> 30:58.857
Subtitle: Paul Carver
